8. Benchmark RDMA/JACCL vs Ring/TCP
Exo includes a benchmark script.
Example:
```bash
uv run bench/exo_bench.py \
  --model Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct-4bit \
  --pp 128,512 \
  --tg 128 \
  --max-nodes 2 \
  --sharding tensor \
  --instance-meta jaccl \
  --repeat 3 \
  --json-out m3u-rdma-results.json
```
Important metrics:
```text
prompt processing tokens/sec
generation tokens/sec
time to first token
peak memory per node
whether both nodes are used
```
Compare:
```text
MlxRing / ring / TCP
vs
MlxJaccl / jaccl / RDMA
```
If JACCL is working correctly, the RDMA path should reduce inter-node overhead.
