9. Lower-Level MLX/JACCL Route
Use this if you want to bypass Exo and test MLX distributed directly.
9.1 Install MLX and MLX-LM
On both Macs:
```bash
python3 -m venv ~/mlx-rdma
source ~/mlx-rdma/bin/activate
pip install -U mlx mlx-lm
```
9.2 Make sure SSH works
From Mac A:
```bash
ssh mac-b.local hostname
```
If needed, enable:
```text
System Settings → General → Sharing → Remote Login
```
on Mac B.
9.3 Generate MLX distributed config
From Mac A:
```bash
mlx.distributed_config --verbose \
  --hosts mac-a.local,mac-b.local \
  --over thunderbolt \
  --backend jaccl \
  --auto-setup \
  --output m3u2-jaccl.json
```
9.4 Launch distributed MLX-LM
```bash
mlx.launch --verbose \
  --backend jaccl \
  --hostfile m3u2-jaccl.json \
  --env MLX_METAL_FAST_SYNCH=1 \
  -- \
  python -m mlx_lm chat \
  --model mlx-community/Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct-4bit
```
For a larger test:
```bash
mlx.launch --verbose \
  --backend jaccl \
  --hostfile m3u2-jaccl.json \
  --env MLX_METAL_FAST_SYNCH=1 \
  -- \
  python -m mlx_lm chat \
  --model mlx-community/Qwen3-235B-A22B-8bit
```
