14. Troubleshooting
`ibv_devices` shows nothing
Run RDMA enable again from Recovery:
```bash
rdma_ctl enable
```
Then reboot.
Exo sees only one Mac
Check both Macs are running Exo with the same namespace:
```bash
EXO_LIBP2P_NAMESPACE=m3u-rdma-cluster uv run exo
```
Also check macOS firewall and local network permissions.
Placement shows Ring instead of JACCL
This usually means MLX/Exo did not find the RDMA path.
Check:
```bash
ibv_devices
```
and rerun the Exo RDMA network script:
```bash
sudo tmp/set_rdma_network_config.sh
```
Small model is slower on two Macs
That is normal. Use one Mac for small models.
Huge model loads but generation is slow
Try:
```text
lower context length
different sharding placement
JACCL instead of Ring
fewer concurrent requests
larger model with MoE active-parameter efficiency
```
